{"version":"1","id":"servlsst","handle":"servlsst","name":"Serverless Status","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/2aca873667ae4638b2d3c450c916c3a6","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-3.2803,"y":-2.8339,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":138,"newest_post_at":"2023-09-28T00:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2019-10-04T00:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":1.720588,"summary_length_avg":272.971014,"title_length_avg":45.123188,"title_length_var":120.397868,"tag_entropy":2.714595,"tag_diversity":0.463768,"top_tag_share":0.224638,"avg_upvotes":0.202899,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.014493,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.103448,"zero_engagement_share":0.905797,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.663815,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.045455},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-7.6176,-4.6324],"cadence_depth":[1.3529,-8.0735],"hype_variety":[-5.9559,-4.6618],"title_style":[-6.0147,-2.0147]},"top_tags":[["serverless",134],["aws",66],["cloud",16],["aws-lambda",14],["cloudflare",10],["database",7],["azure",6],["architecture",6]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["The best of serverless in 2020","Serverless + DOOM = mind blown","Serverless Status Issue 243: May 6, 2022"],"outlier":["Portable serverless, Workers gets cron triggers, and Amazon's serverless time series database"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"keYjKWjtB","title":"Serverless Status Issue 293: September 28, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/293","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-293-september-28-2023-keyjkwjtb","summary":"Serverless Status newsletter will be taking an extended break, but has not closed yet. Cloudflare is introducing a new pricing model for Workers that combines the benefits of their current models. Cooperpress offers other newsletters on JavaScript, frontend, Ruby, Node.js, Go, React, Postgres, and JAMstack.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"EV2XnykxI","title":"Serverless Status Issue 292: September 14, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/292","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-292-september-14-2023-ev2xnykxi","summary":"Serverless Status Issue 292: September 14, 2023. After six years of bringing the latest serverless updates to your inbox, we're in the process of winding things down. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to use Bun on AWS Lambda.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-14T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"aEdmHdhNG","title":"Serverless Status Issue 291: August 31, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/291","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-291-august-31-2023-aedmhdhng","summary":"Datadog\u2019s annual research into the serverless ecosystem has been updated for 2023. Serverless usage continues to rise across all major cloud providers (AWS, Google, Azure) When it comes to managed container-based adoption Google Cloud is out in front. Node and Python remain the most popular languages for AWS Lambda.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-31T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"OmDaibqGv","title":"Serverless Status Issue 290: August 3, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/290","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-290-august-3-2023-omdaibqgv","summary":"The Business of Serverless is an hour-long chat with serverless expert Yan Cui. It covers serverless vs containers, microservices, cost analysis, and even some context on Amazon Prime Video\u2019s architectural change from a strictly serverless approach.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"0AGDsu6R0","title":"Serverless Status Issue 289: July 20, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/289","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-289-july-20-2023-0agdsu6r0","summary":"PolyScale.ai is a fully autonomous distributed database cache at the edge. Supporting both TCP and HTTP, accelerate reads and lower global latency with Cloudlare Workers, Vercel, Deno Deploy or Netlify. This post shares why you may want to look at replacing app code with serverless integrations.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-20T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"KRKZ4pfA1","title":"Serverless Status Issue 288: July 6, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/288","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-288-july-6-2023-krkz4pfa1","summary":"PolyScale.ai is a distributed, serverless database cache with a fully autonomous caching engine. Implement in minutes to accelerate reads and lower global latency for Postgres, MySQL, MariaDB or MS SQL. The Easiest Way to Get Low Latency Database Reads is to get low Latency Reads.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"z1AzQqlOq","title":"Serverless Status Issue 287: June 22, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/287","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-287-june-22-2023-z1azqqloq","summary":"Cloudflare has also released a case study of how Kinsta used Workers and Workers KV to significantly improve cache hit rates. This look at how to build an SAM-based app to run MediaInfo \u2013 a metadata viewer for media files \u2013 on S3 objects at scale.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-06-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"jGfN6tmuw","title":"Serverless Status Issue 286: June 8, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/286","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-286-june-8-2023-jgfn6tmuw","summary":"Ruby, one of Lambda's earliest officially supported languages, gets a long overdue runtime update. Praveen highlights the benefits of upgrading, noting that cold starts are marginally slower, and that 2.7 support has been extended until the end of the year to enable a smooth transition.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-06-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"s5aSRLSFc","title":"Serverless Status Issue 285: May 25, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/285","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-285-may-25-2023-s5asrlsfc","summary":"Cloudflare made a | Irvine-Broque and Silverlock Dynaboard sponsor. Montana Low (PostgresML) Goldman & Zikibayeva (CockroachDB) Alex Ellis Sean Bailey (CocksroachDB), Alex EllisSean Bailey.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-05-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"vpqEGJoTb","title":"Serverless Status Issue 284: May 11, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/284","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-284-may-11-2023-vpqegjotb","summary":"Amazon announced plans to move away from a distributed microservices architecture over to a monolithic app in an effort to help \u201cachieve higher scale, resilience, and reduce costs\u201d This news recently got picked up again, most notably by DHH (of Ruby on Rails fame), and as you might expect plenty of commentary within tech circles, some of which we've shared.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1f352d2ef5dfc504a2e74e400ffb9ba6?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-05-11T00:00:00.000Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"6973-A366","title":"The best of serverless in 2020","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/181","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-best-of-serverless-in-2020-6973-a366","summary":"The trends matched up with other surveys with Lambda, Node, and Python leading the way. Debugging proved the trickiest serverless development task. This continues to ring true to me at the end of 2020 too. We encourage you to take a serverless survey by Coding Sans.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/84bea4477ecdbc99bb7d34768994f283","num_upvotes":9,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2020-12-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"IClrvc9FG","title":"Serverless + DOOM = mind blown","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/201","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-doom-mind-blown-iclrvc9fg","summary":"AWS Step Functions Now Integrates with EventBridge. Step Functions brings the serverless workflow and EventBridge lets you route events between AWS services. Now you can publish events to an EventBridge bus directly from a Step Functions workflow. Unfortunately we just missed this as it came out as we sent the last issue :-)","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4bb2c6ef2674a3cbea292fbb40dd79b5","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2021-05-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"esqOHDjCW","title":"Serverless Status Issue 243: May 6, 2022","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/243","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-243-may-6-2022-esqohdjcw","summary":"Netlify engineer Salma Alam-Naylor breaks down the idea of 'the edge' The 'edge' is about running code as close to an end user as possible. Alam Naylor: We're All Living On It \u2013 But What Exactly is 'The Edge?'","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8d818bcd6cd4254b7209f7c51f86f038","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-05-06T12:59:41.516Z"},{"id":"F44hPAHLJ","title":"Serverless Status Issue 275: January 6, 2023","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/275","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-275-january-6-2023-f44hpahlj","summary":"Serverless Status Issue 275: January 6, 2023 Hello! After a break over the holidays we're back to bring you up to speed on all things serverless in 2023. If you missed our last issue, it was a round-up of some of the biggest and best links we shared in serverless status.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8d818bcd6cd4254b7209f7c51f86f038","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-01-06T14:01:17.799Z"},{"id":"XeLBxiiwP","title":"Serverless Status Issue 269: November 11, 2022","url":"https://serverless.email/issues/269","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-status-issue-269-november-11-2022-xelbxiiwp","summary":"Serverless scheduler is designed to manage and run scheduled tasks at scale all across AWS. It can be used for one-time events or recurrently across many AWS services without the need to manage the infrastructure. You get 1 million'schedules' per AWS account to work with.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8d818bcd6cd4254b7209f7c51f86f038","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-11-28T15:15:44.565Z"}],"similar_handles":["ardlbs","andev","readrust","amygoodchild","chromium"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","horde","on_leuwcq","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"ardlbs","handle":"ardlbs","name":"A